cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  Multimodal Kellgren-Lawrence grading of knee osteoarthritis from paired
  radiographs and quantitative MRI
message: If you use this software, please cite it as below.
type: software
authors:
  - alias: vonKarsteine
    email: vonKarsteine@users.noreply.github.com
repository-code: https://github.com/vonKarsteine/Project-MScEng
license: MIT
version: 7.0.0
date-released: "2026-07-27"
abstract: >-
  Five-class Kellgren-Lawrence grading of knee osteoarthritis from paired X-ray
  and quantitative MRI (T2 and R2 volumes). The work contributes three
  components: Residual-Calibrated Kalman Fusion (RCKF), which recasts
  cross-modal fusion as a Bayesian measurement update so the model estimates per
  case how far the volumetric evidence can be trusted; C-MODES, a dynamic
  ensemble selector trained on out-of-fold risk differentials that learns when to
  route a case away from the default model and when not to; and a
  deployment-oriented quantization-aware training profile that distils the
  full-precision composite into a mixed-precision student under a six-term
  objective, so the quantized model inherits the teacher's cross-modal trust
  policy rather than only its predictions.
keywords:
  - knee osteoarthritis
  - Kellgren-Lawrence grading
  - multimodal fusion
  - ordinal classification
  - Kalman filter
  - ensemble selection
  - quantization-aware training
  - medical imaging
